<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Uclés (1108)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1108</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ucles">Uclés</a> was fought on 29 May 1108 near Uclés in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. An Almoravid army under Tamim ibn Yusuf defeated a Castilian-Leonese force, and Sancho Alfónsez, the only son and heir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a>, was killed. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> then took a line of frontier fortresses south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagus">Tagus</a>, and the succession crisis that followed weakened Castile-León.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ucles-1108.jpg" alt="Battle of Uclés (1108)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tribiwiki · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Campo_batallas_Ucl%C3%A9s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The fall of Toledo prompted the taifa rulers to call in the Almoravids of North Africa, who defeated Alfonso at the Battle of Sagrajas in 1086 and again at the <b>Battle of Uclés</b> in 1108, where his only son Sancho was killed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile · Military</a></li></ul></section>
